# ROS 2 packages (src/)

- `src/` is one colcon workspace on ROS 2 Humble, grouped by domain (see
  [ARCHITECTURE.md](ARCHITECTURE.md)). Each group is code-owned
  ([CODEOWNERS](CODEOWNERS)) — keep changes scoped to your group.
- Build and test only through the wrappers, inside the dev container:
  ```bash
  ./tools/build.sh [-t <group>]     # colcon build --symlink-install
  ./tools/test.sh  [--packages-select <pkg>]
  ```
  `--symlink-install` means Python-only edits need no rebuild.
- New/changed dependencies go in the package's `package.xml`; adding a package or a
  dependency is an "ask first" change.
- **Do not edit vendored packages** under `src/vehicle/**` (vesc, ackermann_mux,
  f1tenth_stack) without coordinating — see
  [src/vehicle/VENDORED.md](src/vehicle/VENDORED.md). They are built but not
  tested/linted.
- Changing `f1tenth_interfaces` messages or `f1tenth_common` is a shared-surface
  change: trace the downstream consumers first (see the contract rule).
